## Rule of the Court (NY Convention recognition under Singapore IAA s 31)
##
## Source:
##   - International Arbitration Act 1994 (2020 Rev Ed), Singapore ("IAA").
##     Section 31 implements Article V of the New York Convention 1958
##     (recognition and enforcement of foreign arbitral awards) for
##     Singapore. The grounds for refusing enforcement that are pleaded
##     in this matter are:
##       s 31(2)(c) — "a breach of the rules of natural justice occurred
##                     in connection with the making of the award by which
##                     the rights of any party have been prejudiced";
##       s 31(2)(d) — "the award deals with a difference not contemplated
##                     by or not falling within the terms of the submission
##                     to arbitration, or contains a decision on a matter
##                     beyond the scope of the submission to arbitration";
##       s 31(4)(b) — "enforcement of the award would be contrary to the
##                     public policy of Singapore".
##   - DKT v DKU [2025] 1 SLR 806 (CA) — four-condition framework for
##     "infra petita" natural justice challenges (point properly before
##     the tribunal; essential to the dispute; tribunal completely failed
##     to consider it; prejudice).
##   - COD v COE [2023] 4 SLR 708 — alternative cases "buried" in
##     pleadings can still be within the submission.
##
## This file expresses the rule applied in:
##   SIC/OA 9/2025 — GNC Holdings LLC v ONI Global Pte Ltd
##                   and LAC Global (Singapore) Pte Ltd
##   Judgment of Chua Lee Ming J, Simon Thorley IJ, James Allsop IJ
##   (delivered by Allsop IJ), 21 October 2025
##   Neutral citation [2025] SGHC(I) 25.
##
## Trace #6 is the first SICC trace and the first to express a
## *partial* refusal of enforcement: Order 3 of the Tribunal's Final
## Award is enforced *except for* sub-paragraphs (d)(ii), (d)(iii) and
## (f), which are excised because the parties were not afforded a
## meaningful opportunity to make submissions on those specific terms.
##
## Methodologically:
##   #1 (formula)              — pure arithmetic
##   #2 (deferred conditional) — temporal predicate
##   #3 (bounded discretion)   — rule strips a filter
##   #4 (composition over findings) — arithmetic + Booleans
##   #5 (conjunctive logical composition) — clauses + witnesses + Ladd
##   #6 (partial statutory refusal) — Boolean disjunction over named
##                                    statutory grounds, *and* a
##                                    sub-order excision list. The
##                                    enforcement decision is no longer
##                                    binary; it returns a *subset* of
##                                    the operative paragraphs.
##
## This is also the first trace whose rule of decision is a different
## *legal family* from the other five (Singapore IAA + NY Convention
## vs DIFC/ADGM English-law-via-statute).
##
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------
## CATALA 1.1.0 NOTES
##
## Statutory grounds and order paragraphs are encoded as enumerations
## (Catala has no `text` primitive). The reasoning shape is:
##
##   for each pleaded ground:
##     defendant supplies a boolean assertion (the ground is made out);
##     court returns one of {Dismissed, AllowedInFull, AllowedInPart};
##   the application is allowed iff *at least one* ground is not
##   Dismissed; the order is varied to remove paragraphs flagged as
##   AllowedInPart.

```catala
declaration enumeration GroundId:
  -- G1_PublicPolicy_S31_4_b
  -- G2_NaturalJustice_S31_2_c
  -- G3_OutsideScope_Damages_S31_2_d
  -- G4_PartialOrder3_S31_2_c_d

declaration enumeration GroundOutcome:
  -- Dismissed
  -- AllowedInFull
  -- AllowedInPart

declaration enumeration Order3Para:
  -- Para_a
  -- Para_b
  -- Para_c
  -- Para_d_i
  -- Para_d_ii
  -- Para_d_iii
  -- Para_e
  -- Para_f
  -- Para_g

declaration enumeration ApplicationDisposition:
  -- ApplicationDismissedEntirely
  -- ApplicationAllowedInPart
  -- AwardSetAside

declaration structure GroundFinding:
  data ground content GroundId
  data defendant_made_out content boolean
  data court_outcome content GroundOutcome

declaration structure ParaFinding:
  data para content Order3Para
  data tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics content boolean

declaration structure Disposition:
  data n_grounds_pleaded content integer
  data n_grounds_dismissed content integer
  data n_grounds_partial content integer
  data n_grounds_full content integer
  data application_disposition content ApplicationDisposition
  data award_enforced content boolean
  data n_paras_excised content integer

declaration scope CompositeJudgment:
  input grounds content list of GroundFinding
  input order3_paras content list of ParaFinding
  output disposition content Disposition
  output excised_paras content list of Order3Para
  output enforced_paras content list of Order3Para

scope CompositeJudgment:
  ## Excise an Order 3 paragraph iff the Tribunal did *not* hear the
  ## parties on its specific terms — the partial-refusal logic from
  ## paras 103-107 of the judgment.
  definition excised_paras equals
    map each p among order3_paras
    such that not p.tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics
    to p.para
  definition enforced_paras equals
    map each p among order3_paras
    such that p.tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics
    to p.para
  definition disposition equals
    let dismissed equals
      number of (list of g among grounds
                 such that g.court_outcome = Dismissed)
    in
    let partial equals
      number of (list of g among grounds
                 such that g.court_outcome = AllowedInPart)
    in
    let full equals
      number of (list of g among grounds
                 such that g.court_outcome = AllowedInFull)
    in
    let pleaded equals number of grounds in
    let app equals
      if full > 0 then AwardSetAside
      else (if partial > 0 then ApplicationAllowedInPart
            else ApplicationDismissedEntirely)
    in
    Disposition {
      -- n_grounds_pleaded: pleaded
      -- n_grounds_dismissed: dismissed
      -- n_grounds_partial: partial
      -- n_grounds_full: full
      -- application_disposition: app
      -- award_enforced: full = 0
      -- n_paras_excised:
           number of (list of p among order3_paras
                      such that not p.tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics)
    }
```

## Test — facts of SIC/OA 9/2025

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestGNCHoldings:
  composite scope CompositeJudgment
  output disposition content Disposition
  output excised_paras content list of Order3Para
  output enforced_paras content list of Order3Para

scope TestGNCHoldings:
  definition disposition equals composite.disposition
  definition excised_paras equals composite.excised_paras
  definition enforced_paras equals composite.enforced_paras

  ## The four grounds of resistance to enforcement (paras 14, 16).
  ## Defendants asserted each ground was made out; the court ruled.
  ##
  ## Ground 1 — public policy (spoliation/fraud), s 31(4)(b).
  ##   Court held no public-policy violation: the Tribunal thoroughly
  ##   addressed the spoliation evidence (paras 148-184).
  ## Ground 2 — natural justice, s 31(2)(c).
  ##   DKT v DKU four-condition framework not satisfied (para 182):
  ##   the "take back Singapore" argument was not properly before the
  ##   Tribunal as a separate issue, was not essential, was considered,
  ##   no prejudice. Claim fails (para 184).
  ## Ground 3 — outside scope, s 31(2)(d) (damages).
  ##   Court held the alternative damages case fell within the pleadings
  ##   as understood under COD v COE (paras 135-138).
  ## Ground 4 — outside scope / natural justice on Order 3 sub-paragraphs,
  ##   s 31(2)(c) and (d). Court held the Tribunal was authorised to
  ##   fashion a just regime for cl 13.4 generally (paras 99-102), but
  ##   did not afford the parties an opportunity to be heard on certain
  ##   specific sub-paragraphs (paras 103-105). Allowed in part (para 107).
  definition composite.grounds equals [
    GroundFinding {
      -- ground: G1_PublicPolicy_S31_4_b
      -- defendant_made_out: false
      -- court_outcome: Dismissed
    };
    GroundFinding {
      -- ground: G2_NaturalJustice_S31_2_c
      -- defendant_made_out: false
      -- court_outcome: Dismissed
    };
    GroundFinding {
      -- ground: G3_OutsideScope_Damages_S31_2_d
      -- defendant_made_out: false
      -- court_outcome: Dismissed
    };
    GroundFinding {
      -- ground: G4_PartialOrder3_S31_2_c_d
      -- defendant_made_out: true
      -- court_outcome: AllowedInPart
    }
  ]

  ## Order 3 of the Tribunal's Final Award (para 752 of the FA).
  ## A paragraph is excised iff the Tribunal did *not* hear the
  ## parties on its specific terms (paras 103-105).
  definition composite.order3_paras equals [
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_a      -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: true  };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_b      -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: true  };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_c      -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: true  };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_d_i    -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: true  };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_d_ii   -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: false };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_d_iii  -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: false };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_e      -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: true  };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_f      -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: false };
    ParaFinding { -- para: Para_g      -- tribunal_heard_party_on_specifics: true  }
  ]

  ## --- Court holdings, transcribed from para 185(a)-(c) ---
  ## (a) "the application by the Defendants ... is allowed in part as
  ##     set out in (b) and (c) below, but is otherwise dismissed."
  assertion disposition.application_disposition = ApplicationAllowedInPart
  ## (b) "HC/ORC 1222/2025 be varied such that the parts of the
  ##     orders of the Tribunal in Order 3(d)(ii) and Order 3(d)(iii)
  ##     ... and Order 3(f) ... not be enforced."
  assertion disposition.n_paras_excised = 3
  ## (c) "The orders of the Tribunal otherwise set out in para 752 of
  ##     the Final Award be enforced." => the Award itself stands.
  assertion disposition.award_enforced = true
  ## Three of the four grounds were dismissed.
  assertion disposition.n_grounds_dismissed = 3
  ## One ground was allowed in part.
  assertion disposition.n_grounds_partial = 1
  ## No ground was fully allowed.
  assertion disposition.n_grounds_full = 0
```
